{#- #885, out of #87: the partner programme, rented from Rewardful. #1361
    (operator, 21 Oct 2026: "a simple page on /refer or something on the
    website that explains how it works (and is wired-up to Rewardful)") lit
    the page for good: it explains the programme and carries the terms
    whether or not the key is set, and /refer/ answers 301 to it
    (netlify.toml). What the key still decides (src/_data/rewardful.js) is
    the script and the referral on checkout, which stay dark without it; what
    the signup URL decides is the one way in:

      REWARDFUL_SIGNUP_URL set   the "Sign up as a partner" button
      otherwise                  the waitlist form (#1362, operator 21 Oct
                                 2026: "a 'join waitlist' form that people can
                                 submit before I start paying Rewardful")

    The waitlist is a Netlify Form, the contact form's idiom (#456): the name
    in the POST body, the honeypot, a success page the build really writes
    (src/partners-thanks.njk). It collects an email address and what the
    person does, and privacy §03 says so; test/partner-waitlist.test.js holds
    the form to that list.

    The shape (operator, 21 Oct 2026, the same night): "just the headline
    'get 20%' * terms apply (12 months limitation), then the form (needs to be
    clearer not so blended into the background), then more information ...
    Clear CTA, easy to sign up, not a page full of text and then some form at
    the very bottom." So: the number, one line, the fine print; the form in a
    white card with bordered fields; three short steps; the terms last.

    The rate, the twelve months and the thirty-day hold are set inside
    Rewardful by #886 and quoted here; the cookie window and the attribution
    rule are set there too, which is why rule 3 states no number of days.
    English only, like the legal pages: these are terms, and a translation
    of terms is a compliance job, not a catalogue entry. -#}

<header class="page-hero partner-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">partners</span>
    <h1 class="page-h1 partner-h1">Get 20%.<a class="partner-star" href="#terms" aria-label="Terms apply">*</a></h1>
    <p class="page-lede">Of everything a client you refer pays Prospektor, for their first twelve months.</p>
    <p class="partner-fine">* Terms apply: 20% of each paid invoice, for twelve months from the client's first payment. <a href="#terms">The terms</a>.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="partner-join">
  <div class="partner-card" id="waitlist">
    {%- if rewardful.signup %}
    <h2 class="partner-card-h2">Become a partner</h2>
    <p class="partner-card-lede">Sign up and you get a link of your own. Rewardful runs the programme for us: your link, your clicks and your balance are all there.</p>
    <p class="partner-card-cta"><a class="btn-cta btn-wide" href="{{ rewardful.signup }}" rel="noopener">Sign up as a partner</a></p>
    {%- else %}
    <form class="contact-form partner-waitlist" name="partner-waitlist" method="POST" action="/partners/thanks/"
          netlify netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
      <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="partner-waitlist">
      <h2 class="partner-card-h2">Join the waitlist</h2>
      <p class="partner-card-lede">The programme opens with its first partners. We write to you when your link is ready.</p>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <label class="contact-label" for="waitlistEmail">Your work email</label>
        <input class="contact-input" id="waitlistEmail" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@yourcompany.com" required>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-row">
        <label class="contact-label" for="waitlistRole">What you do</label>
        <select class="contact-input" id="waitlistRole" name="role" required>
          <option value="" selected disabled>Choose one</option>
          <option value="agency">I run outbound for clients</option>
          <option value="fractional">I lead sales for clients, fractionally</option>
          <option value="consultant">I consult or build automations for clients</option>
          <option value="other">Something else</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <input type="text" name="bot-field" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" style="position:absolute;left:-9999px;" aria-hidden="true">
      <p class="partner-card-cta"><button class="btn-cta btn-wide" type="submit">Join the waitlist</button></p>
    </form>
    {%- endif %}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section partner-how">
  <div class="partner-how-inner">
    <h2 class="section-h2 partner-how-h2">How it works</h2>
    <ol class="partner-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="partner-step-n">1</span>
        <h3>Get your link</h3>
        <p>{% if rewardful.signup %}Sign up above{% else %}Join the waitlist above{% endif %} and your link is yours. Rewardful runs the programme: your clicks and your balance are there.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="partner-step-n">2</span>
        <h3>Send it to a client</h3>
        <p>They buy Prospektor through your link, by the month or the year up front. The first partner link a buyer used is the one that counts.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="partner-step-n">3</span>
        <h3>Get paid</h3>
        <p>20% of every invoice they pay, for twelve months. Each line is payable thirty days after its invoice is paid, through Rewardful.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="partner-agency">Running Prospektor for your own clients? An agency that pays for the workspaces it runs gets 20% off each one instead. A workspace earns one of the two: the discount, or the share.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section partner-terms-section" id="terms">
  <div class="legal-inner">
    <h2 class="section-h2">The terms</h2>
    <ol class="partner-terms">
      <li>You cannot refer yourself: not your own domain, your own workspace, your own card, or an address at your company.</li>
      <li>A company that has ever had a workspace cannot be referred. Deleted counts as ever.</li>
      <li>The first partner link a buyer used is the one that counts. One partner per workspace.</li>
      <li>A workspace you pay for at 20% off does not also earn 20% back.</li>
      <li>No ads on our name, and no coupon sites.</li>
      <li>We can end a partnership and cancel unpaid earnings if the rules are broken.</li>
      <li>Earnings become payable thirty days after the invoice they come from is paid, and are paid out through Rewardful.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="partner-note">Your link and your balance are in Rewardful, which runs the programme for us. What its cookie records, and how to switch it off, is in <a href="/privacy/#cookies">the privacy notice</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>
